Facts found (read first):
1. **What Jev is:** `typesafe-ai/jev` on the Vercel AI Gateway, called through `experimental_evaluate` from `ai@7.0.105` (jev.ts:14/:26). It returns **typed answers only** (boolean / choice / score, each with probabilities) plus `usage.inputTokens`. It returns no prose, so "the argument" must come from a writer model (claude.js `callClaude` :205). The AI writes the words; Jev and the stats make the numbers.
2. **Every call site is an off-server script** (C31): build-manager-archetypes.mjs:166-173 (`--jev`, paid-run gated :124-130), news-line/jev_{league_chat,presser_signals,transactions,coach_decisions,garbage_time,luck_plays,narrative,yt_triage}.mts, live-market/jev_live_plays.mts:227, luck/jev_luck.mts, model-lab/jev_research_auditor.mts. **The server never calls Jev.** It only reads stored outputs: `manager_archetype_jev` (manager-archetypes.js:86, writer `storeJevAnswers` :1425), `jev_chat_signals` (bluff-detector.js:131, coach/people/variables.js:310), and the persona block (counterparty-pricing.js:201-266, :342, :429; routes/trades.js:329 strips the raw values).
